# Dooers Agent Starter — rules for AI assistants

## Architecture (mandatory)

- **Handler** in `src/modules/agent/agent.py` — async generator with `yield send.*`; normalizes audio/images/documents.
- **Workflow** in `workflow.py` — `Runner.run_streamed` on one agent; streams `tool_call`/`tool_result`/`reasoning`; execution guard; guardrails.
- **One agent** built in `core/agent.py`. No per-domain agents or handoffs.
- **Tools**: `core/tool_catalog.py` (contract) + `core/tools.py` (implementation) + `ALL_TOOLS`.
- **Skills**: `skills/*.md` (frontmatter `id/name/description/requires_tools`) or Studio upload. Procedures live here, not in code.
- **Prompt**: `core/policies.py` is static (creator settings only). Volatile state → `core/context.py::RuntimeContext.state_message()`.
- **Settings UI** in `schemas.py`; **env** in `config.py` (+ `.env.example`, `env.prod.example`).
- **HTTP routes** only in `main.py` — no business logic there.

## Platform contract

- LLM via **Dooers Gateway** (`DOOERS_GATEWAY_API_KEY`, Chat Completions wire). No vendor chat keys in Studio.
- Knowledge via **managed Dooers RAG** (`src/modules/rag/`). Tools using `dooers.tools.rag` must call `rebind_execution_context` first.
- Attached documents via `src/modules/doc_processing/` + tool `get_thread_document_context`.
- Persistence only through the SDK (`memory`, `settings`, `await agent_server.database()`).
- Every turn: `send.run_start()` … `send.run_end()`; tolerated errors → `record_soft_failure`.
- Package: `dooers-agents-server[dooers,observability]>=0.23`.

## Best practices (developer agents)

- **Credentials:** ask whether the user has an account; env vs settings vs chat form; explain auth formats. Never hardcode keys. Recipe: `docs/recipes/external-service-credentials.md`
- **Test before push:** `uv run poe check && uv run poe test` (+ optional `poe dev`) before suggesting `dooers push`
- **Audiences:** branch by `organization_role` / `workspace_role` / `channel` inside tools or Skills

## Do NOT

- Commit secrets (`.env`, `env.prod`, service-account JSON)
- Add agents/handoffs for business domains; put date/user/documents in `policies.py`
- Reimplement WebSocket protocol, WhatsApp HMAC, thread storage or vector stores
- Reference private Dooers codebases — only this starter and public packages

## When adding features

| Feature | Files to touch |
|---------|----------------|
| Procedure / policy | `skills/<id>.md` |
| Action / integration | `core/tool_catalog.py`, `core/tools.py`, `src/modules/external/<svc>/`, `schemas.py` for credentials |
| Studio field | `schemas.py` (+ `tests/test_schema_and_llm.py` if code depends on it) |
| Form | tool marker + `send.form()` in `agent.py` (`docs/recipes/feedback-form.md`) |
| Chart | `yield send.chart(...)` |
| External channel | `dispatch()` in `channels/` |

## Code style

- Python 3.11+, ruff (line-length 140, rules E/F/I/UP/B/SIM); run `uv run poe check`
- Tool functions: validate args, business errors as text, compact output, `ctx.context.record_tool_call(name)`

